In article <1992Jan29.042403.7645@midway.uchicago.edu> mehr@oskar.uchicago.edu (David Mehringer) writes:
>In article <20382@hacgate.UUCP> hayes%bh_ddemo3@hac2arpa.hac.com writes:
>>Regarding genociding monsters:
>>What is the best monster to genocide?
>>What is the best class of monsters to genocide?
>>
>This, of course, depends on your present stock of items and
>intrinsics.  If you don't have magic resistance (and don't plan
>on getting it soon) I suggest liches (L) or if your scroll is
>not blessed, starting with master lich, then demi lich.

Liches, particularly master liches, are one of the most heinous monsters in
the game.  I thoroughly approve of genociding them.  Vampire lords have a way
of cursing items, or so I believe, so I tend to genocide them if I get a
chance.  If I used a wish to get 3 blessed scrolls of genocide, I finish it
off with rust monsters, just 'cuz they peeve me so much.

And one of my favorite things to do if I have Excalibur/Stormbringer and a
character to match--read a cursed scroll of genocide and use it to summon a
passel o' wraiths.  They aren't that dangerous if they can't drain level, and
there's nothing like gaining five levels from eating corpses (they're
practically non-nutricious, so chow 'em as soon as you can).  And wishing for
three cursed scrolls of genocide can practically double your level, hit
points, and spell points, and levels add to your chance to hit.

One of these days, I'll find the Wizard out of explore mode....
